    "task_id": "ceremony-trim-r647-s1-qa-prepare-diagnostics",
    "goal": "Make a failed QA prepare stage locatable: the failed Assurance result states the conditions prepare ran under and a bounded stderr tail, while the check stage and every persisted record stay free of verifier output.",
    "acceptance": [
      {
        "id": "CT-S1-A1",
        "assertion": "Meet T1 and D2 in docs/specs/ceremony-trim-r647.spec.md: when the prepare command ends in timeout, nonzero exit or output limit, the failed Assurance result carries the execution conditions (isolated delivery, fresh home and cache directories, no worktree node_modules), the declared timeout, and a stderr tail of at most 2048 bytes taken from the end with control characters other than newline and tab removed. A failing check stage returns none of these. The Loop contract states the stage-specific rule in place of the blanket no-output sentence.",
        "verification": "{\n  \"contract\": \"assurance_kernel/verification_descriptor/v2\",\n  \"command\": {\n    \"executable\": \"bun\",\n    \"argv\": [\n      \"test\",\n      \"tests/qa-prepare-diagnostics.test.ts\"\n    ],\n    \"cwd\": \".\",\n    \"timeout_ms\": 300000,\n    \"max_output_bytes\": 196608\n  },\n  \"environment\": {\n    \"prepare\": null,\n    \"writable_paths\": []\n  }\n}\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "CT-S1-A2",
        "assertion": "Meet invariants I1 and I2: the stderr tail is absent from QaCheckDiagnostic entries, from batch failure facts, and from the stored TaskRecord after a failed run; existing assertions that strip injected output fields still hold.",
